{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"Notice that we were asked to find the one-sided limit, $\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to -1^-}g(x)$. This is the limit where $x$-values approach $-1$ from the left.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's find the limit as $x$ approaches $-1$ from the left. We will use the fact that $g(x)=e^x$ for $x$-values smaller than $-1$.\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to -1^-}g(x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to -1^-}e^x\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=e^{-1}\u0026\\gray{\\text{Direct substitution}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{e}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, we found that $\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to -1^-}g(x)=\\dfrac{1}{e}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"$g(x)=\\begin{cases}\ne^x\u0026\\text{for }-5\u003cx\u003c-1\n\\\\\\\\\n\\dfrac xe\u0026\\text{for }-1\\leq x\u003c0\n\\end{cases}$\n\n**Find $\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to -1^-}g(x)$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$-\\dfrac1e$","correct":false},{"content":"$0$","correct":false},{"content":"$\\dfrac{1}{e}$","correct":true,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"The limit doesn't exist.","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
